      "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"group\"><h4>Questions 22–26</h4><p>Complete the summary. Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.</p><h5>How the eyes of ocean creatures have developed differently from those of land creatures</h5><div class=\"question-item\" id=\"q9-anchor\"><p><strong>22</strong> Ocean creatures&#x27; eyes have developed many different <input type=\"text\" id=\"q9\" name=\"q9\" aria-label=\"Question 22\" autocomplete=\"off\"> according to the depth of the water where they live. Ocean roaming predators have well developed eyesight because they hunt where there is plenty of light. However, light only reaches the <input type=\"text\" id=\"q10\" name=\"q10\" aria-label=\"Question 23\" autocomplete=\"off\"> of some sea creatures of the deep via fibre-optic cables, and by 50 feet deep, <input type=\"text\" id=\"q11\" name=\"q11\" aria-label=\"Question 24\" autocomplete=\"off\"> is the only colour which is visible. At a depth of around <input type=\"text\" id=\"q12\" name=\"q12\" aria-label=\"Question 25\" autocomplete=\"off\"> , no light from the sun can get through. At this level, the only source of light is that which is produced through <input type=\"text\" id=\"q13\" name=\"q13\" aria-label=\"Question 26\" autocomplete=\"off\">.</p></div></div>",
      "sourceTaskId": "task.b007.p2-060.summary.q22-26"
